ENG-12, ENG-15  Native full screen: the program is told the size it has, and a window smaller than the screen keeps its size and is scaled up.
Component: lby-trixie-fullscreen (patches/lby-trixie-fullscreen/).
Merged 2026-11-15 from 0006-winemac-native-fullscreen-reports-its-size.patch (ENG-12) and 0007-winemac-native-fullscreen-scales-a-small-window.patch (ENG-15); the tree they give is the same.

dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m (winemac.so). Lullaby, 2026-10-27 and 2026-10-28. LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

== ENG-12 ==
What: a window the engine lets scale (presentationScalable: a program that refused a resize, or a borderless window
shown as a window) keeps Wine's size and fits it into the real one. Native full screen is below the menu bar and notch
(1512x949 points on a 14" MacBook Pro), the program's borderless window was the whole screen (1512x982): the engine fitted
982 into 949 (scale 0.966), left a black strip at the side and a stale line at the bottom, and the program never heard of
its new size (windowDidResize posted the size Wine already believed in). Now, in native full screen and outside a drag,
windowDidResize posts the real frame (fullscreen = TRUE). The program gets its WM_SIZE, answers with setFrameFromWine, and
the stage is 1:1 again. Leaving full screen posts the old frame as before (windowWillExitFullScreen).
Used by: windowstate asking a borderless covering window for native full screen (S12).
Other bases: stock Wine has no scaling stage; the patch is for Dormison's cocoa_window.m only.
Test: RE9 (D3DMetal) goes to native full screen: HUD 3024x1898, picture fills the screen, no side strip
(layer-dump: no 0.966 transform); ETS2, PEAK and Isaac unchanged.
Verified on: see ledger (2026-10-27).
Switch: LULLABY_FULLSCREEN_SIZE=0 keeps the scaled picture; on by default.


== ENG-15 ==
What: a game that runs in a window of its own size (1920x1200 chosen in its settings, a 960x600 point window on a 3024x1964 screen)
and is put into native full screen by windowstate or the green button was told by the engine its window had become the size of
the screen (windowDidResize posts the real frame), so it made a swapchain of the screen's size (Unity PEAK: 3024x1833) and, on
leaving, saved that size over the one the player had chosen. Now, when a window goes to native full screen (windowWillEnterFullScreen)
and Wine's own frame is smaller than the screen (less than the screen's width, or more than 40 points shorter than its height),
the window becomes scalable (presentationScalable, as for a window the program refuses to resize) and keeps its Wine frame: the
program is not told the new size, the stage fits its picture into the full screen (the engine's own scaler, pointer included), and
the resolution the game saved stays the one the player chose. A window that covered the screen (RE9, ETS 2 borderless) is not
touched: ENG-12 still tells it the real size. Leaving full screen (or failing to enter it) puts the window back as it was.
The same holds when the program changes its size while in native full screen (a resolution chosen in the game's settings):
a size smaller than the screen becomes scaled (followFullscreenScaling, called from setFrameFromWine; the real frame stays the
screen's), the screen's size again ends the scaling and ENG-12 reports as before.
The two parts work together: ENG-15 skips the size report of ENG-12 for such a window.
Other bases: Dormison's cocoa_window.m only.
Test: PEAK (Unity, Vulkan) saved at 1920x1200 in a window, native full screen on: HUD at 1920x1200 with the picture filling
the screen, Player.log keeps "InitializeOrResetSwapChain 1920x1200", the registry keeps 1920x1200 after exit; RE9 still 3024x1898.
PEAK switched in game from 3024x1964 to 1920x1200 in native full screen: the picture fills the screen (before: a small window in the middle).
Verified on: see ledger (2026-10-28).
Switch: LULLABY_FULLSCREEN_SCALE=0 (or LULLABY_FULLSCREEN_SIZE=0) as a launch option gives the old behaviour; on by default.


